Babet 2.6.0 roadmap
====================

[ ] Evaluate libarchive and define the multi-format archive API.
[ ] Add secure TAR inspection and extraction.
[ ] Add deterministic TAR creation.
[ ] Add .tar.gz/.tgz, .tar.xz, .tar.bz2 and .tar.zst support.
[ ] Define safe handling for standalone gzip/xz/bzip2/zstd streams.
[ ] Replace or complement std::regex in babet.find with bounded matching
    (RE2 and/or a safe glob mode).
[ ] Introduce shared strict Lua validation helpers without changing public
    contracts.
[ ] Consider archive creation from explicit file lists and exclusion rules.
[ ] Audit code, tests, FR/EN documentation, examples and PDF manuals before
    release, using the same standard as 2.5.0.

Deferred ideas retained in notes.md:
- parent-side PATH resolution followed by execve;
- worker-to-worker channels;
- cooperative cancellation design;
- macOS/BSD portability.
